    <bpmn:process id="W_W3969" name="W3969. Philippine Competition Commission (PCC) Relationship &amp; Engagement Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Maintained relationship; PCC inquiry/guidance; policy consultation
Frequency: Ongoing
Volume: Enterprise PCC relationship
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Participants: Legal (links to VS-100), Govt Affairs (links to VS-104), CEO/CFO, affected business leads, external counsel
Source: workflow W3969 — Philippine Competition Commission (PCC) Relationship &amp; Engagement Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3969_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3969_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3969_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3969_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3969_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3969_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3969_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3969_Start3" name="Maintained relationship; PCC inquiry/guidance; policy consultation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3969_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3969_Task4" name="VP Legal own the PCC relationship: a single accountable point of contact…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Legal own the PCC relationship: a single accountable point of contact, awareness of current PCC priorities/guidelines/enforcement trends, participation in PCC public consultations (links to VS-104), and engagement of qualified external competition counsel on retainer
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Legal / Govt Affairs
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3969_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3969_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3969_Task5" name="VP Legal maintain the inquiry-response playbook and dawn-raid plan (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Legal maintain the inquiry-response playbook and dawn-raid plan (links to W3970), the records/legal-hold interface (links to VS-88/W3970), and the privilege protocol for competition-sensitive advice
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3969_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3969_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3969_Task6" name="VP Legal/CEO escalate any PCC inquiry/investigation to the Board Audit/Risk…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Legal/CEO escalate any PCC inquiry/investigation to the Board Audit/Risk Committee (links to VS-36) and activate matter management (links to VS-100)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / CEO
Accountable (A): Board Audit Committee
Duration: On event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3969_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3969_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3969_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3969_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-619 (ensure controlled execution — Competition Authority (PCC) Engagement, Investigation &amp; Remediation (PA-129.3).) | - operational: single accountable contact; operational: privilege protocol
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
