    <bpmn:process id="W_W3971" name="W3971. PCC Investigation, Preliminary Inquiry &amp; Motu Proprio Matter Defense" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PCC preliminary inquiry, formal investigation, or motu proprio (own-motion) case
Frequency: On event
Volume: Rare but high-impact
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Participants: Legal, external competition counsel, affected business unit, Compliance (links to VS-119), Finance (links to VS-17.4), Govt Affairs (links to VS-104), CEO
Source: workflow W3971 — PCC Investigation, Preliminary Inquiry &amp; Motu Proprio Matter Defense</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3971_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3971_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3971_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3971_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3971_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3971_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3971_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3971_Start3" name="PCC preliminary inquiry, formal investigation, or motu proprio (own-motion) case">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3971_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3971_Task4" name="VP Legal/external-counsel conduct the matter defense: factual investigation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Legal/external-counsel conduct the matter defense: factual investigation (internal interviews, document review, data analytics), legal analysis (no-infringement / no-effect / exemption defenses), and response to the Statement of Objections / PCC preliminary determination
Responsible (R): VP Legal / External Counsel / Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per matter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3971_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3971_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3971_Task5" name="VP Legal manage the matter lifecycle: evidence and privilege management (links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Legal manage the matter lifecycle: evidence and privilege management (links to VS-88), internal communications controls, board reporting (links to VS-36), and decision on leniency/settlement vs full defense (links to W3972)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / CEO
Accountable (A): Board Audit Committee
Duration: Per matter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3971_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3971_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3971_Task6" name="VP Legal prepare for PCC adjudication and any subsequent appeal (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Legal prepare for PCC adjudication and any subsequent appeal (links to W3973); coordinate settlement/commitment options (links to W3972) and disclosure (links to W3974)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / External Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per matter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3971_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3971_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3971_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3971_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-619 (ensure controlled execution — Competition Authority (PCC) Engagement, Investigation &amp; Remediation (PA-129.3).) | - operational: external counsel and analytics; operational: communications plan (links to VS-14)
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
