    <bpmn:process id="W_W3972" name="W3972. Leniency, Settlement &amp; Commitment (Whistleblower) Program Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Detected cartel/serious conduct; PCC offer of settlement/commitment; strategic leniency application
Frequency: On event
Volume: Rare
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Participants: VP Legal, external competition counsel, CEO, Board Audit Committee, Compliance (links to VS-119), affected executives/staff
Source: workflow W3972 — Leniency, Settlement &amp; Commitment (Whistleblower) Program Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3972_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3972_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3972_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3972_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3972_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3972_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3972_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3972_Start3" name="Detected cartel/serious conduct; PCC offer of settlement/commitment; strategic leniency…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3972_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3972_Task4" name="VP Legal/external-counsel assess leniency/marker eligibility for any detected…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Legal/external-counsel assess leniency/marker eligibility for any detected cartel conduct (price-fixing, bid-rigging, market/customer allocation) and decide whether to file a leniency/marker application with the PCC for immunity/reduced fines, coordinating with speak-up (links to VS-119)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / External Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO / Board Audit Committee
Duration: On event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3972_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3972_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3972_Task5" name="VP Legal assess settlement vs full-defense vs commitment options during a PCC…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Legal assess settlement vs full-defense vs commitment options during a PCC matter, weighing fine reduction, conduct-change obligations, admission scope, and downstream private-action exposure
Responsible (R): VP Legal / External Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per matter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3972_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3972_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3972_Task6" name="VP Legal execute the chosen path (leniency cooperation, settlement agreement…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Legal execute the chosen path (leniency cooperation, settlement agreement, or binding commitments), manage the obligations, and document the decision basis (links to records VS-88)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / External Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per matter + ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3972_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3972_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3972_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3972_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-619 (ensure controlled execution — Competition Authority (PCC) Engagement, Investigation &amp; Remediation (PA-129.3).) | - operational: rapid assessment on detection; operational: careful scoping
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance</bpmn:text>
